{
  "title": "113: Al-Falaq الفلق",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nقُلْ اَعُوْذُ بِرَبِّ الْفَلَقِۙ‏(1)\nQUL A-OO’ZO BE RABBIL FALAQ.\nSay: ‘‘I seek refuge in the Lord of the Dawn\nمِنْ شَرِّ مَا خَلَقَۙ‏(2)\nMIN SHARRE MAA KHALAQ.\nFrom the evil of what He hath created\nوَمِنْ شَرِّ غَاسِقٍ اِذَا وَقَبَۙ‏(3)\nWA MIN SHARRE GHAASEQIN EZAA WAQAB.\nFrom the evil of the dark night when it overtaketh\nوَمِنْ شَرِّ النَّفّٰثٰتِ فِى الْعُقَدِۙ‏(4)\nWA MIN SHARRIN NAFFAASAATE FIL O’QADE.\nAnd from the evil of blowing on knots (of the malignant witchcraft)\nوَمِنْ شَرِّ حَاسِدٍ اِذَا حَسَدَ‏(5)\nWA MIN SHARRE HAASEDIN EZAA HASAD.\nAnd from the evil of the envious when he envieth!",
  "merits": "This is a ‘Madani’ Surah and it has 5 verses. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that whoever recites this Surah in the month of Ramazan in any of his prayers, it is as if he has fasted in Makkah and he will get the reward for performing Hajj and Umrah.\nImam Muhammad al-Baqir (a.s.) said that in the prayer of Shaf’ (in Salaatul-layl) one should recite Surah al-Falaq in the first rak’aat and an-Naas in the second."
}
